# CRUD actions require authorization

## Package recommendation

When both CRUD and Authorization are installed: loading a record in a CRUD action is not permission. Apply `authorize` / policy checks and query scoping consistent with the app’s Authorization setup.

## Required behavior

- Scope index queries (CRUD beforePaginate / finder) to what the identity may see.
- Authorize view/edit/delete subjects before mutating or exposing them.
- Keep policies on Authorization’s side; CRUD listeners may call authorize/scope but must not invent a parallel ACL.
- Do not assume Authentication APIs from this integration alone.

## Anti-patterns

- IDOR via CRUD get-by-id without policy/scope
- Duplicating AuthZ rules inside CRUD listeners as the only check
